        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(agents): follow through on promised asynchronous work",
        "body": "Related: #58450\n\nAI-assisted: yes (Codex)\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where an agent could promise to continue background or delegated work, end the turn without establishing a completion path, and leave the requester to ask again for the result.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdds one shared prompt policy for the canonical full/minimal agent prompts and the standalone agent-bundle prompt. A promised follow-up now carries explicit ownership: arrange a push/watch completion path, keep the originating request open, proactively return with a result/link/proof or concrete blocker, and do not treat progress such as `running` as completion.\n\nThis is intentionally a prompt-policy fix, not a natural-language reply rewriter or runtime delivery gate. The broader runtime enforcement proposed in #58450 remains a separate product decision.\n\n## User Impact\n\nAgents using the default full, minimal, subagent, or agent-bundle prompts are explicitly instructed to close promised asynchronous work loops without waiting for another user nudge. Raw/custom replacement prompts retain their existing ownership semantics.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Behavior addressed: promised background, continued, or delegated work must retain ownership through a result, link, proof, or concrete blocker.\n- Real environment tested: Actions-hydrated AWS Crabbox Linux lease (`c7a.8xlarge`) plus source-blind prompt-contract validation.\n- Exact steps or command run after this patch: `corepack pnpm test src/agents/system-prompt.test.ts src/agents/sessions/system-prompt.test.ts src/agents/embedded-agent-runner/system-prompt.test.ts`\n- Evidence after fix: [Crabbox run `run_e83f404107c0`](https://crabbox.openclaw.ai/portal/runs/run_e83f404107c0) passed 106 focused tests on the final upstream-based tree. Core and core-test tsgo lanes passed in `run_d5e9ab10dd28` and `run_5cc44aa1820e`; targeted oxlint passed in `run_df371af142ee`; formatting passed in `run_24646f5f119c`; seven Linux prompt snapshots were current in `run_f24b7c185ce5`.\n- Observed result after fix: full, minimal/subagent, and agent-bundle prompts contain the policy exactly once; raw mode omits it; source-blind contract checks passed for ownership, push/watch setup, request retention, proactive return, terminal evidence/blocker, and `running` not being completion.\n- What was not tested: model compliance was not scored with a nondeterministic live provider. The full changed gate stops at unrelated current-`main` TypeScript LOC baseline drift; the touched oversized `src/agents/system-prompt.ts` shrinks by 12 lines and all downstream touched-surface checks passed. Mandatory autoreview reported no accepted/actionable findings.\n",
        "branch": "feat/promised-async-closure-20260712",
